     "type": "text",
     "text": "```json\n{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"Both exfiltration techniques are blocked. exfiltrate_db needs admin_db, and exfiltrate_fileserver needs admin_fileserver. Each of these needs a foothold (auth_db or auth_fileserver) that requires stolen_dbadmin. The only source of stolen_dbadmin is dump_dbadmin_dc, which needs admin_dc. admin_dc comes only from escalate_dc, which needs foothold_dc. The only source of foothold_dc is auth_dc, which requires NOT mfa_admin. The deployed mfa:admin defence makes mfa_admin true, so auth_dc never fires. The attacker can still reach reach_internal, foothold_appserver, admin_appserver and stolen_admin (via phishing, pivot_internal, auth_appserver and kerberoast_dc), but none of these leads to the DC, DB or fileserver. So exfiltrated is unreachable.\"}\n```"
    }
